{title: O Day of Rest and Gladness}
{artist: Christopher Wordsworth / German folk melody}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: G}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: o-day-of-rest-and-gladness.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (O_Day_Of_Rest_And_Gladness-Woodbird)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]O [Em]day of [G]rest and [D]gladness,
[Bm]O [C]day [Am]of [D]joy and [G]light,
[G]O [Em]balm of [G]care and [D]sadness,
[Bm]Most [C]beau[Am]ti[D]ful, most [G]bright;
[G]On thee, the high [Em]and [A]low[D]ly,
[C]Through [G]a[D]ges [Bm]joined [Em]in [A]tune,__[D]__
[D]Sing [C]Ho[G]ly, [Am]holy, [D]holy,
[Bm]To [C]God, [Am]the [D]great Tri[G]une.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]On [Em]thee, at [G]the cre[D]ation,
[Bm]The [C]light [Am]first [D]had its [G]birth;
[G]On [Em]thee, for [G]our sal[D]vation,
[Bm]Christ [C]rose [Am]from [D]depths of [G]earth;
[G]On thee, our Lord [Em]vic[A]tor[D]ious,
[C]The [G]Spi[D]rit [Bm]sent [Em]from [A]Heav’n,__[D]__
[D]And [C]thus [G]on [Am]thee most [D]glorious
[Bm]A [C]tri[Am]ple [D]light was [G]giv’n.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Thou [Em]art a [G]port pro[D]tected
[Bm]From [C]storms [Am]that [D]round us [G]rise;
[G]A [Em]garden [G]inter[D]sected
[Bm]With [C]streams [Am]of [D]para[G]dise;
[G]Thou art a cool[Em]ing [A]foun[D]tain
[C]In [G]life’s [D]dry, [Bm]drea[Em]ry [A]sand;__[D]__
[D]From [C]thee, [G]like [Am]Pisgah’s [D]mountain,
[Bm]We [C]view [Am]our [D]promised [G]land.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Thou [Em]art a [G]holy [D]ladder,
[Bm]Where [C]an[Am]gels [D]go and [G]come;
[G]Each [Em]Sunday [G]finds us [D]gladder,
[Bm]Near[C]er [Am]to [D]Heav’n, our [G]home;
[G]A day of sweet [Em]ref[A]lec[D]tion,
[C]Thou [G]art, [D]a [Bm]day [Em]of [A]love,__[D]__
[D]A [C]day [G]of [Am]resur[D]rection
[Bm]From [C]earth [Am]to [D]things a[G]bove.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]To[Em]day on [G]weary [D]nations
[Bm]The [C]heaven[Am]ly [D]manna [G]falls;
[G]To [Em]holy [G]convo[D]cations
[Bm]The [C]sil[Am]ver [D]trumpet [G]calls,
[G]Where Gospel light [Em]is [A]glow[D]ing
[C]With [G]pure [D]and [Bm]ra[Em]diant [A]beams,__[D]__
[D]And [C]liv[G]ing [Am]water [D]flowing,
[Bm]With [C]soul [Am]re[D]freshing [G]streams.
{end_of_verse}
